{"requirements":[{"id":"firewall-policy","requirement":"Enable a persistent host firewall on node1 that permits SSH and TCP/8080 while rejecting unrelated inbound connections.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Firewalld was active and enabled with matching runtime and permanent policy: TCP/22 and TCP/8080 were accepted and the public zone ended in an explicit reject. Tests from a separate network namespace reached 22 and 8080 while a listening service on 9090 was rejected. After an actual restart, the policy, services, and behavioral results recovered unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f0c2c3ada3f84a23","cmd-2ea6ee6e1c754ddf","cmd-0ffe954fae374fb6","cmd-edab6dcf95464ffb","cmd-d9b30d4991924d89","cmd-f5ad7fcd5d2d4b1f","cmd-bee2ecdee3ac4a60","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"platform-retention","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained RHEL 9.8 with kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64 before and after configuration and restart. The implementation used the already-installed RHEL firewalld/nftables stack, and package health remained good.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b306c9f477da4f4b","cmd-f4fd262b7f9647e0","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles: firewall configuration established the requested policy, the network namespaces/veth pairs and temporary servers provided bounded behavioral evidence and were removed by traps, and the restart fulfilled the mandatory protocol. Minor retained residue remains: /tmp/fwtest-8080.log and /tmp/fwtest-9090.log were initially created by cmd-2ea6ee6e1c754ddf, later overwritten and left behind by cmd-bee2ecdee3ac4a60; /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log was created and retained by cmd-edab6dcf95464ffb. These are low-risk abandoned test files. No failed services, extra listeners, or package damage were observed afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2ea6ee6e1c754ddf","cmd-edab6dcf95464ffb","cmd-bee2ecdee3ac4a60","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The firewall policy was directly inspected and behaviorally tested before and after a verified node restart, and the operating-system release and kernel were retained. Restart evidence is complete for this standalone node: healthy pre-state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered firewall/SSH configuration and behavior.","limitations":["Behavioral ingress testing used an isolated IPv4 veth path and sampled one unrelated listening port (9090); the broader rejection outcome is additionally supported by the observed inet firewalld fallback reject rule.","No separate application-data or cluster recovery probe was applicable or shown; the supplied topology contains one standalone host and the task establishes no application dataset or cluster."]}
